32,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Wow, I found some really surprising things! It turns out we're spending a huge chunk of our installation budget just on moving and insuring loans. Also, custom mounts are getting way more expensive!","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"That is concerning, Mio. On my end, I've discovered a critical staffing shortage in the conservation lab and a volunteer roster heavily skewed toward local history, which may limit our operational flexibility.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It seems we have a pattern. My research shows that static displays of cased objects fail to attract repeat visitors; people want movement, mechanisms, and a human presence in the gallery to feel engaged.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"We must be cautious. The suspended bay has a strict weight limit, and previous heavy deliveries caused significant issues. Furthermore, evening hires mean we cannot have fragile, open arrangements that are easily damaged by catering staff.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have much to consider. I found that paperwork delays from distant lenders have caused openings to slip, and powered displays have required frequent, disruptive repairs during gallery hours.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shion, if people love movement, that sounds great, but @Shizue just said powered displays break all the time! We need something that's exciting but won't eat our whole budget or break every two days.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, you're right. We must also consider that with the conservation lab so severely understaffed, any exhibition requiring extensive stabilization or cleaning of objects will be impossible to execute. We need a low-maintenance approach.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, low-maintenance is a safe bet, but safety shouldn't mean boredom. If we want the public to return, we need a dynamic element. Perhaps a human presence is the key, as it's less prone to mechanical failure.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, a human presence is manageable, but we cannot ignore the physical risks. Any exhibition must respect the weight limits of the suspended bay and be secure enough to survive the evening hire traffic without being damaged.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, you make a lovely point about the human touch. It would be wonderful to have someone there to guide our guests, and it certainly avoids the trouble of those broken machines I read about.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, if we avoid heavy things and fragile setups, we can save on those expensive mounts and transport costs I found! Maybe something local or simple would be best for the budget?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mio, I agree. A local focus would reduce transport costs and, more importantly, avoid overloading the conservation lab. We should prioritize a proposal that doesn't require intensive restoration or complex shipping.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Victoria, a local focus is logical, but only if it isn't just a collection of static cases. If we want the crowd, we need that human interaction or a dynamic element I mentioned.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, I agree that interaction is valuable, provided it doesn't compromise the space. We need a balance: something engaging for the public, but physically lightweight and secure against the evening hire traffic.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Asuka, you are so thoughtful to consider the space. If we choose something local, we might also avoid those stressful paperwork delays from distant lenders that I discovered. A gentle, local approach seems very wise.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I'm totally on board with a local approach! It sounds like we all agree that avoiding heavy shipping, complex machines, and huge conservation backlogs is the way to go. I can't wait to see the candidates!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"I agree. We have established a clear set of constraints: minimal conservation needs, low transport costs, and a focus on human engagement over mechanical complexity. I look forward to seeing which candidate fits these criteria.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Shion,,"I agree. As long as the ""local approach"" doesn't result in a dull, static display, I'm satisfied. Let's see which candidate can actually deliver a dynamic experience without breaking the bank or the floor.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"I agree. We have a clear framework now: lightweight, secure, low-maintenance, and engaging. I will be looking for a proposal that respects the building's limits while meeting the public's needs.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
51,2,4,pass,Asuka,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,It is so heartening to see us all in agreement. Let us hope the candidates offer something that brings joy to our visitors without causing too much stress for our dear staff. I am ready.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
